                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "93b582ef-1f46-3468-9e0b-b8f8e4d6992f",
                        "entry_id": "615902d4-4210-3340-adef-d06bf4110643",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор., разг. в дореволюционной России: агент полиции"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fa74dea1-0ede-3fab-a909-50dc7c380e09",
                        "entry_id": "615902d4-4210-3340-adef-d06bf4110643",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. непоседа, шалун, озорник"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0260705b-9011-46c5-ac81-1df70e143163",
                                "sense_id": "fa74dea1-0ede-3fab-a909-50dc7c380e09",
                                "text": "И было это заведение вроде зверинца: архаровцы, скандалисты, обломы; все как на подбор — самые развращённые мальчишки."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "692f58d3-53e3-3db9-8ee7-36cb799e7d16",
                        "entry_id": "615902d4-4210-3340-adef-d06bf4110643",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. отчаянный, беспутный человек; озорник, буян, головорез"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c84e169e-6463-45ef-afbd-58dc94c2c94f",
                                "sense_id": "692f58d3-53e3-3db9-8ee7-36cb799e7d16",
                                "text": "Пошёл в церковь, народу тьма-тьмущая. У двери стоят архаровцы с большущими ножами и то и дело толкают народ да бьют их кулаками."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ba78d7e1-d9e3-3224-80c3-cc5872e9bb02",
                        "entry_id": "615902d4-4210-3340-adef-d06bf4110643",
                        "glosses": [
                            "прост. жулик, мошенник, вор"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d98171ca-c59c-4f16-afef-6470ce980084",
                                "sense_id": "ba78d7e1-d9e3-3224-80c3-cc5872e9bb02",
                                "text": "— Я уж не знаю, что мне с этими архаровцами и делать. Слов моих они не слушают, драться с ними у меня силушки нет, а они всё тащат, всё тащат: кто что зацепит, то и тащит."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fa19238c-13df-4d30-9655-3ae3811a9754",
                        "source_entry_id": "615902d4-4210-3340-adef-d06bf4110643",
                        "source_sense_description": "агент полиции",
                        "target_lang_word": "ruffian",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ruffian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4545a38d-970b-3dfb-98d7-a5de8ee4ea31",
                                        "entry_id": "f95dc807-922b-3345-aa9f-99c71dec31df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A scoundrel, rascal, or unprincipled, deceitful, brutal and unreliable person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "279382b7-c0c7-4a5e-aacc-b7d1dfe047f9",
                                                "sense_id": "4545a38d-970b-3dfb-98d7-a5de8ee4ea31",
                                                "text": "What wilt thou on thy death-bed play the Ruffian?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51aa71ce-118e-49d0-91fc-67739bd28e10",
                                                "sense_id": "4545a38d-970b-3dfb-98d7-a5de8ee4ea31",
                                                "text": "It was at Count Siloszech's. He'd heard her sing in the streets, with a tall, black-bearded ruffian, who accompanied her on a guitar, and a little fiddling gypsy fellow. She was a handsome woman, with hair down to her knees, but stupid as an owl."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bd1dc2ad-4586-3ce4-ad7f-6e731220364c",
                                        "entry_id": "f95dc807-922b-3345-aa9f-99c71dec31df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pimp; a pander."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a2ae5664-df69-3aed-a68c-ef72176cf456",
                                        "entry_id": "f95dc807-922b-3345-aa9f-99c71dec31df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lover; a paramour."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35432afe-e715-4ea1-969c-53ec781f55e2",
                                                "sense_id": "a2ae5664-df69-3aed-a68c-ef72176cf456",
                                                "text": "He [her husband] is no sooner abroad than she is instantly at home, revelling with her ruffians."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ruffian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "edc701d8-2f18-36be-95cc-a1e5dd89a214",
                                        "entry_id": "c64ef0f8-d29c-391a-a809-f49b69729c62",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To play the ruffian; to rage; to raise tumult."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29d16ff9-ddc8-4403-a089-092126f7c899",
                                                "sense_id": "edc701d8-2f18-36be-95cc-a1e5dd89a214",
                                                "text": "Methinks the wind does speak aloud at land; A fuller blast ne'er shook our battlements. If it hath ruffianed so upon the sea."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ruffian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3ed765fb-7dbc-3755-8706-29998df147ed",
                                        "entry_id": "f383f8bc-07e8-31b4-b4bc-a87e05a3b459",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Brutal, cruel, ruffianlikes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "776e3af9-568e-44f8-953b-2204a62c149c",
                                                "sense_id": "3ed765fb-7dbc-3755-8706-29998df147ed",
                                                "text": "ruffian rage"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "093d4dec-c957-4f91-bc29-ab24254faacc",
                        "source_entry_id": "615902d4-4210-3340-adef-d06bf4110643",
                        "source_sense_description": "агент полиции",
                        "target_lang_word": "hoodlum",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hoodlum",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "509e3195-35bd-3d5e-a011-7562223ae678",
                                        "entry_id": "1d9967df-7cd0-350f-b660-d4846b88e890",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A gangster; a hired thug."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6aaa9ac-def6-410e-b6c6-38f215b93dbd",
                                                "sense_id": "509e3195-35bd-3d5e-a011-7562223ae678",
                                                "text": "There is no question the MS-13 gang must be stopped. It is a vile organization of hoodlums with no regard for life."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2a34fe6-4e43-4f03-9b84-a53f3aacb178",
                                                "sense_id": "509e3195-35bd-3d5e-a011-7562223ae678",
                                                "text": "In Sam Mendes's excellent gangster movie Road to Perdition (2002), he tested the boundaries further playing a hitman – but while we know he's a killer, we never really see him go full-pelt hoodlum."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da196fb1-8f7d-407f-8c0a-14a21ddf424f",
                                                "sense_id": "509e3195-35bd-3d5e-a011-7562223ae678",
                                                "text": "Caesar Enrico “Rico” Bandello is a hoodlum who rises swiftly in Chicago’s mob world, in the 1931 film “Little Caesar.” Played by Edward G. Robinson, Rico is tracked down by police and shot."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "39afee49-f75e-4cbe-ae83-88a1a929d49e",
                                                "sense_id": "509e3195-35bd-3d5e-a011-7562223ae678",
                                                "text": "The state’s police spokesman Wasiu Abiodun told CNN in a statement that operatives arrested 11 armed “hoodlums” who set fire to a government building after looting it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "528e9f62-cc2f-3e04-b0aa-aeb2b907e6ea",
                                        "entry_id": "1d9967df-7cd0-350f-b660-d4846b88e890",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rough or violent youth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
